From 872c813f746961b9aa23db76e3713e33fe336a86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Audia <therealgraysky@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 14:17:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Replace sudo with a scoped polkit rule for service
 control

Drop sudo from the privileged path entirely: the web process now calls
systemctl directly and systemd asks polkit to authorize the request.

This removes sudo and the shell from the privileged path and keeps the
same tight scoping the sudoers file had.

Debian packaging ships the rule in /usr/share/polkit-1/rules.d/,
depends on polkitd | policykit-1, and removes the sudoers file left
behind by earlier versions on upgrade. JS polkit rules are supported on
the whole v2 baseline (Debian 12 ships polkit 122).
---
